msgid "Templates"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A template is a board that holds only lists — no cards and no labels. "
"When you start the same kind of project again and again, such as a weekly"
" sprint or a client onboarding, a template saves setting the lists up "
"every time."
msgstr ""

msgid "Creating a template"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the :guilabel:`Templates` section of the boards overview, click "
":guilabel:`New Template`, give it a name and click **Save**. It opens "
"like any board, marked :guilabel:`Template`."
msgstr ""

msgid "A template with four empty lists."
msgstr ""

msgid "A template."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Add, rename, recolour and reorder its lists exactly as on a board (see "
":doc:`boards`). Lists on a template have no **+** button, because a "
"template has no cards. Give the template and its lists the colours you "
"want new boards to start with."
msgstr ""

msgid "Using a template"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When you create a board, choose the template in the :guilabel:`Template` "
"box of the :guilabel:`Create a new Board` dialog (see :doc:`boards`). The"
" new board gets:"
msgstr ""

msgid "a copy of the template's lists, in the same order;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the board and list colours *you* chose on the template. Anyone else gets "
"their own colours, or the default."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The board and the template are independent from then on: changing the "
"template later doesn't change boards already made from it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Templates other people shared with you are offered too, marked with their"
" owner's name."
msgstr ""

msgid "The template menu"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A template's tile has the same menu as a board's (see :doc:`boards`), "
"with one addition:"
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Duplicate`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Make a copy of the template, under a new name. The copy is a new template"
" that only you can see: it gets the lists and your own colours, but not "
"the people the original is shared with."
msgstr ""

msgid "There are two differences in what you can do with a template:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It can only be shared with people who already have a KanbanMF account, "
"never by e-mail invitation."
msgstr ""

msgid "It has no e-mail notifications, since it has no cards."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":guilabel:`Archive Template` moves it to the archived boards, where "
":guilabel:`Restore Template` brings it back and :guilabel:`Delete "
"Template` deletes it permanently. Boards made from it are not affected."
msgstr ""

